BUG#22 — Aider wizard integration: spawn tab + sentinel + auto-relaunch
Reproduced and fixed on VM (vm-test, michal-VirtualBox), 2026-05-11.

Code surfaces touched:
  bterminal/app.py
    +open_aider_wizard_tab(session_config, on_done) — spawns
      tools/aider_setup_wizard in a fresh TerminalTab; binary
      discovery mirrors open_wizard_tab (memory_wizard pattern).
      Tab tagged is_aider_wizard_tab=True so the close hook can
      identify it. child-exited → _on_aider_wizard_done.
    +_on_aider_wizard_done(wizard_tab, on_done) — reads sentinel
      via aider_probe.read_sentinel, builds new aider config via
      aider_probe.compute_relaunch_config, spawns aider tab as
      a normal ai_config session, deletes sentinel file.
  bterminal/providers/aider_probe.py
    +SENTINEL_PATH constant (~/.config/bterminal/.aider_wizard_done.json)
    +read_sentinel(path=None) — parse with graceful None on
      missing / malformed JSON; returns dict otherwise.
    +compute_relaunch_config(payload, original_config) — pure
      function the App-side calls. Returns a new config dict (with
      provider_options.model = sentinel.model) when sentinel
      matches original.session_id; None otherwise.
  bterminal/ui/terminal_tab.py
    ~_aider_resolve_missing_model — action="wizard" now defers
      app.open_aider_wizard_tab via GLib.idle_add (necessary —
      modal dialog response handler ignores set_current_page).
    -_aider_show_wizard_placeholder — removed (was BUG#21 stub).

